<div class="py-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-10" data-page="guide"><div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto"><span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Gujarat Composting Masterclass</span><h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">6-Phase Complete Field Guide</h1><p class="text-slate-400 mt-2 text-sm sm:text-base">Scientifically proven protocols calibrated for Gujarat’s semi-arid summers and torrential monsoon rains.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6 gap-3"><button data-step="1" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-600 to-teal-700 text-white border-emerald-400 shadow-xl shadow-emerald-950/60 scale-[1.02]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-200">Phase 01</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Selecting Your Composter &amp; Microclimate Placement</span></button><button data-step="2" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-white/[0.03] border-white/10 text-slate-300 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-white/[0.06]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-400">Phase 02</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Mastering the 2:1 Carbon to Nitrogen Ratio</span></button><button data-step="3" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-white/[0.03] border-white/10 text-slate-300 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-white/[0.06]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-400">Phase 03</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Lasagna-Style Layering &amp; Microbial Inoculation</span></button><button data-step="4" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-white/[0.03] border-white/10 text-slate-300 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-white/[0.06]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-400">Phase 04</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Moisture Control &amp; Aeration Dynamics</span></button><button data-step="5" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-white/[0.03] border-white/10 text-slate-300 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-white/[0.06]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-400">Phase 05</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Gujarat Seasonal Protocols: Summer Heat &amp; Monsoon</span></button><button data-step="6" class="p-4 rounded-2xl border text-left transition-all cursor-pointer flex flex-col justify-between bg-white/[0.03] border-white/10 text-slate-300 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-white/[0.06]"><span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold block mb-2 text-emerald-400">Phase 06</span><span class="text-xs font-black line-clamp-2 leading-tight font-display">Harvesting, Sifting &amp; Restoring Gujarat Soils</span></button></div><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 01</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Selecting Your Composter &amp; Microclimate Placement</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Choose the optimal composter volume and location for Gujarat homes, avoiding excessive 44°C summer heat and monsoon flooding.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>In Gujarat's warm semi-arid to coastal climate, container choice and location dictate microbial survival. Direct exposure to 44°C+ summer heat dehydrates bacteria, while unshielded monsoon downpours drown piles into anaerobic sludge.</p><p>Apartment balconies in Ahmedabad, Surat, and Vadodara thrive with compact terracotta stacks or airtight Bokashi systems that occupy under 2 square feet.</p><p>Terraces and residential compounds benefit from dual-chamber tumblers, which speed up decomposition via effortless mechanical rotation without hand turning.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Place in partial shade with morning sun and complete protection from harsh afternoon heat.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Elevate the base by 2 inches using patio bricks to ensure free drainage during rainy months.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Maintain an easily accessible countertop caddy so kitchen scrap collection is second nature.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button disabled data-step="1" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">01 / 06</span><button data-step="2" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></div><template id="guide-template-1"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 01</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Selecting Your Composter &amp; Microclimate Placement</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Choose the optimal composter volume and location for Gujarat homes, avoiding excessive 44°C summer heat and monsoon flooding.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>In Gujarat's warm semi-arid to coastal climate, container choice and location dictate microbial survival. Direct exposure to 44°C+ summer heat dehydrates bacteria, while unshielded monsoon downpours drown piles into anaerobic sludge.</p><p>Apartment balconies in Ahmedabad, Surat, and Vadodara thrive with compact terracotta stacks or airtight Bokashi systems that occupy under 2 square feet.</p><p>Terraces and residential compounds benefit from dual-chamber tumblers, which speed up decomposition via effortless mechanical rotation without hand turning.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Place in partial shade with morning sun and complete protection from harsh afternoon heat.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Elevate the base by 2 inches using patio bricks to ensure free drainage during rainy months.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Maintain an easily accessible countertop caddy so kitchen scrap collection is second nature.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button disabled data-step="1" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">01 / 06</span><button data-step="2" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template><template id="guide-template-2"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 02</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Mastering the 2:1 Carbon to Nitrogen Ratio</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Balance wet Nitrogen-rich kitchen scraps with dry Carbon-rich materials to ensure rapid, sweet-smelling microbial breakdown.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>Composting is cellular digestion executed by trillions of aerobic bacteria and fungi. They burn Carbon for energy and consume Nitrogen to synthesize cellular proteins.</p><p>"Greens" provide Nitrogen, moisture, and quick heat. Examples include raw vegetable peels, melon rinds, rinsed chai tea leaves, and tender garden prunings.</p><p>"Browns" provide Carbon, structural stability, and microscopic air voids. Dry neem leaves, shredded corrugated cardboard, dry coconut pith, and wood shavings are exceptional Browns.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Golden rule: For every bowl of wet kitchen scraps, top with two equal bowls of crushed dry Browns.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Dice tough melon rinds and cauliflower stalks into 1-inch chunks to multiply microbial surface area.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Keep a dry container of shredded cardboard or dry leaves directly beside your compost bin.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button data-step="1" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">02 / 06</span><button data-step="3" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template><template id="guide-template-3"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 03</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Lasagna-Style Layering &amp; Microbial Inoculation</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Construct a self-aerating vertical stack that triggers thermophilic heat and prevents pest attraction.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>Build your pile like an Italian lasagna. Always construct a 3-inch porous foundation layer using coarse brown twigs, coconut husks, or dry stalks at the bottom of the bin.</p><p>Follow with a 2-inch layer of moist kitchen greens. Dust lightly with a handful of garden soil or finished compost—this introduces billions of native decomposer microbes.</p><p>Immediately blanket the surface with dry browns. Never leave exposed fruit sugars on top, which summon vinegar fruit flies.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Dust cold-pressed organic neem cake powder between layers to repel maggots naturally.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Never press down or compact the pile; loose organic geometry is crucial for airflow.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Moisten dry brown layers with a fine mist if they feel bone-dry to the touch.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button data-step="2" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">03 / 06</span><button data-step="4" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template><template id="guide-template-4"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 04</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Moisture Control &amp; Aeration Dynamics</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Conduct the wrung-out sponge test and turn the core regularly to sustain aerobic breathing bacteria.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>Aerobic microbes breathe free oxygen and travel through an ultra-thin moisture film surrounding organic particles. If water fills the air voids, anaerobic bacteria take over, generating sour odors.</p><p>Perform the simple Hand Squeeze Test wearing garden gloves: scoop matter from 6 inches deep and squeeze firmly. Exactly 1 to 2 droplets of water should form between your knuckles.</p><p>Aerate weekly using a spiral corkscrew aerator or pitchfork. Moving outer matter into the hot core accelerates digestion dramatically.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>If it drips multiple streams: excess moisture! Add dry shredded cardboard strips immediately.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>If it crumbles dry: sprinkle 200ml water or diluted sour buttermilk (chhas) to stimulate bacteria.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Aerating once weekly cuts curing time from 16 weeks down to 6 weeks.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button data-step="3" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">04 / 06</span><button data-step="5" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template><template id="guide-template-5"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 05</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Gujarat Seasonal Protocols: Summer Heat &amp; Monsoon</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Weatherproof your bin against scorching 45°C heatwaves and torrential monsoon downpours.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>Gujarat features intense environmental swings: scorching dry summers (exceeding 44°C in Ahmedabad, Rajkot, and Gandhinagar) followed by fierce monsoon downpours.</p><p>During scorching summer months, microbes dry out quickly. Shield bins with green shade cloth and lay a wet burlap jute sack on top of the pile to conserve moisture.</p><p>During the Monsoon, torrential rains can flood open bins within minutes. Keep bins sheltered under balcony overhangs and adjust brown ratios to 3:1 to absorb atmospheric humidity.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Summer: Add 100ml diluted sour buttermilk once weekly to reinforce lactic acid cultures.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Monsoon: Keep lid locked and ensure ground runoff cannot backflow into drainage ports.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Winter: Prime composting weather across Gujarat; turn twice weekly for rapid thermophilic heat.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button data-step="4" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">05 / 06</span><button data-step="6" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template><template id="guide-template-6"><div class="bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-2xl grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8" id="guide-panel"><div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6"><div><span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 tracking-wider">Phase 06</span><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white font-display mt-1">Harvesting, Sifting &amp; Restoring Gujarat Soils</h2></div><p class="text-base text-emerald-200 font-medium bg-emerald-500/10 p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20">Determine maturity, sift black gold humus, and rebuild low-organic-carbon soils across Gujarat.</p><div class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-light"><p>Finished compost is dark chocolate brown, pleasantly crumbly, and smells like fresh forest soil after first rain. Individual scrap remnants are fully decomposed.</p><p>Let the batch cure undisturbed for 14 days after active heat subsides. This allows beneficial mycorrhizal fungi to establish stable humic acids.</p><p>Pass the cured compost through a 1/4-inch wire sieve. Toss coarse un-decomposed seed pits back into your active bin as bio-inoculants.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-4 bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-5 flex flex-col justify-between"><div><h4 class="text-sm font-black text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-display"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.017 2.814a1 1 0 0 1 1.966 0l1.051 5.558a2 2 0 0 0 1.594 1.594l5.558 1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.966l-5.558 1.051a2 2 0 0 0-1.594 1.594l-1.051 5.558a1 1 0 0 1-1.966 0l-1.051-5.558a2 2 0 0 0-1.594-1.594l-5.558-1.051a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.966l5.558-1.051a2 2 0 0 0 1.594-1.594z"></path><path d="M20 2v4"></path><path d="M22 4h-4"></path><circle cx="4" cy="20" r="2"></circle></svg>Field Directives &amp; Checklist</h4><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Perform the Methi Sprout Test: plant 5 fenugreek seeds in a cup of compost; if they sprout green in 3 days, it is completely cured!</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Blend 30% cured compost with 70% garden soil for potting mixes, raised beds, and terrace gardens.</span></li><li class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 flex items-start gap-2.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-check w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg><span>Steep 2 cups of finished compost in 5 liters of water for 24 hours to brew potent foliar compost tea.</span></li></ul></div><div class="pt-4 border-t border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs"><button data-step="5" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-white disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Previous</button><span class="font-mono text-slate-400">06 / 06</span><button disabled data-step="6" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 hover:bg-emerald-400 disabled:opacity-30 cursor-pointer">Next Phase</button></div></div></div></template>
